diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index f53d2fc6e..e07857744 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -110,3 +110,24 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - ci: npx -y uw-harness verify returned 404 from the npm registry on 2026-11-01 (package not published). The new harness.yml workflow will fail until uw-harness is published; it was not run on GitHub. Locally the check was run with the uw-harness source checkout and passed.
 - local-env: PostgreSQL support (DB_TYPE=pgsql, compose profile pgsql) was written but not run. Only MySQL was verified. The full gate drops and reinstalls the local database each time, and needs host port 3306 free because the mysqli driver ignores other ports.
 - full-gate: The full gate does not build the DocBook guides or the SOAP WSDL HTML (documentation.yml needs Publican and xsltproc, not available as composer/npm dependencies). Everything else from CI (lint, api:validate, api:generate, all four PHPUnit suites) is in composer run check.
+
+## 2026-11-01: Collect the checks on uploaded files (issue #36861)
+
+**Changed**
+
+- `file_ensure_uploaded()` in `core/file_api.php` now does all checks on one uploaded file, in a fixed order: antispam, empty name, PHP upload error (any code other than `UPLOAD_ERR_OK`), name length, file type, empty `tmp_name`, readability, empty file, maximum size. A file array without an `error` key is valid (REST files have none).
+- `file_add()`, `IssueAddCommand`, `IssueFileAddCommand`, `IssueNoteAddCommand` (during validation, for each file) and `proj_doc_update.php` call it. The duplicated checks were removed from these places.
+- New `file_filter_not_selected()`: the commands remove the entries that web forms send for an empty file input (`name` empty and `UPLOAD_ERR_NO_FILE`) before they check the files.
+- `proj_doc_update.php` no longer ignores web server upload errors (before, a file with an upload error was skipped and only the title was saved).
+- `ERROR_FILE_NAME_TOO_LONG` now maps to HTTP 400 in `error_map_api_error_to_http_status()` (it gave 500).
+- Tests: `tests/Mantis/FileEnsureUploadedTest.php`, plus REST tests in `RestIssueTest` and `RestIssueNotesTest`.
+
+**Learned**
+
+- `IssueAddCommand` needs the SOAP `mci_*` helpers, so it is easier to test through the REST suite than in `tests/Mantis/`.
+- `MantisCoreBase::login()` makes assertions, so `@doesNotPerformAssertions` gives a risky test, and the full gate reports it.
+- To test `antispam_check()`, set `$g_allow_signup` in `$GLOBALS` and clear `$g_cache_config_eval['g_allow_signup']`; it is a global option and `config_set()` cannot change it.
+
+**Left**
+
+- SOAP `mci_file_add()` (`api/soap/mc_file_api.php`) writes the content itself and does not use `file_add()`; it keeps its own type and size checks.
